%% The life of a memory. Nothing becomes a fact until you apply a reviewed
%% proposal. Any pending or stale proposal can be discarded. Applying a forget
%% also clears every saved proposal. An applied proposal stays listed, marked
%% stale, until you discard it.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    Pending: Pending proposal
    Stale: Stale proposal
    Current: Current fact
    Change: Change proposal (correct or forget)
    Superseded: Superseded (kept as history)
    Forgotten: Forgotten
    Recovery: Recovery required

    [*] --> Pending: propose (files you choose)
    [*] --> Pending: session hook at Stop (opt-in)
    Pending --> Pending: review (read only)
    Pending --> Current: apply (each new fact signed)
    Pending --> Stale: another change applied first
    Stale --> Pending: propose again
    Pending --> [*]: discard
    Stale --> [*]: discard
    Current --> Change: correct or forget
    Superseded --> Change: forget
    Change --> Superseded: apply correction
    Change --> Current: replacement becomes current
    Change --> Forgotten: apply forget (clears all proposals)
    Change --> Recovery: apply interrupted
    Recovery --> Superseded: recover
    Recovery --> Forgotten: recover

    note right of Forgotten
        Record removed. A signed, ID-only
        revocation blocks exact re-import.
    end note
